From 496997989e37b124dc2743ea8dd4df4ddde12ee7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 05:25:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 48/93] kosmickrisp: gate pending timeline waits before Metal
 submission

Use on-demand common submission for unsatisfied timeline waits so Metal cannot retire a native event wait before the host signals it. Move reusable binary payloads correctly and stop the worker before device resource destruction.

Answer VK_SYNC_WAIT_PENDING with whether a signal operation has been submitted rather than whether it completed. Track the highest value already signalled on the CPU or enqueued on the queue's Metal timeline, and treat a binary semaphore wait as pending because its signal must have been submitted first. Otherwise the common runtime reads every unfinished dependency as unsubmitted: it turns the assisted submission worker on for the life of the device and blocks the caller of vkQueueSubmit, which on a virtualized device is the thread that must deliver the release the worker is waiting for.

Keep absolute CPU wait deadlines while observing device loss, wake queue drains when submission fails, and allow lost-device cleanup of pending submissions. Cover delayed host signals, mixed binary waits, loss during waits and drain, a binary wait queued behind a host-gated batch, and submission that outruns a long GPU dependency.
